# claudebox settings: copy to ~/.config/claudebox/cbox.env
# (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/claudebox/cbox.env) and uncomment what you need.
# Every setting is optional; the values shown are the defaults or examples.
# The file is sourced as a shell script, so $HOME and the like work.
#
# These are the settings you are likely to change. The README's settings table
# lists all of them, including folders and ports you rarely need to move.

# ─── agent ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The agent a session starts: claude or opencode (per session: cbox oc).
# CBOX_AGENT=claude

# Show all output: updates, sync messages, MCP relay status (per session: cbox -v).
# CBOX_VERBOSE=0

# Keep this computer awake while a session runs, so long agent runs are not
# paused by sleep: 1 = always, ac = only on mains power (a laptop on battery
# sleeps as usual), 0 = never. Per session: cbox --awake / cbox --no-awake.
# Linux checks the power source when the session starts; WSL: no effect.
# One cbox.env for several machines (dotfiles): ac suits desktops and laptops.
# CBOX_AWAKE=0

# ─── container ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Settings marked "cbox reset" apply to newly created containers.

# Memory of each container. A project's .cbox can set its own
# ([container] memory = 8g), e.g. for several agents. cbox reset
# CBOX_MEMORY=4g

# Files and folders in the project the container sees empty: name or *.ext
# (anywhere), dir/ (a folder), a/b (from the project root), !pattern (keep).
# Unset: safe mode hides .env, .env.*, *.pem, *.key and private SSH keys;
# normal mode hides nothing. Once set, it applies to both modes. cbox reset
# CBOX_MASK=".env .env.* !.env.example *.pem secrets/"

# Mount .git/config and .git/hooks read-only, so code in the container cannot
# plant commands git would run on the Mac. 0 = writable. cbox reset
# CBOX_PROTECT_GIT=1

# Folders of your real ~/.config shared read-only into the container's
# ~/.config. Code in the container can read them: leave out folders with
# tokens (gh, gcloud). cbox reset
# CBOX_SHARE_CONFIG="opencode nvim"

# A .zshrc the container sources (read-only).
# CBOX_ZSHRC="$HOME/.zshrc"

# SSH folder mounted as ~/.ssh (normal mode). Use a folder with only the keys
# containers may use, not your personal ~/.ssh. With a warden ssh resource,
# the keys stay on the Mac and only config, known_hosts and *.pub are mounted.
# CBOX_SSH_DIR="$HOME/.ssh/claudebox"

# ─── network ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Hosts a safe container may reach besides the defaults (the agents' APIs,
# npm, PyPI, GitHub): host, *.domain (subdomains only) or host:port.
# CBOX_EGRESS_ALLOW="openrouter.ai *.example.com registry.example.com:8443"

# ─── credentials (warden) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# macOS keychain for warden's secrets: a name in ~/Library/Keychains or a path.
# cbox warden secret set writes there; warden looks there first, then in the
# keychain search list. Unset: the default keychain (usually login).
# CBOX_KEYCHAIN="$HOME/Library/Keychains/shared.keychain-db"

# ─── Claude accounts (cbox account) ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Shown with the renewal steps when an account's token nears its year
# (<name> = the account's name), e.g. where you keep your tokens.
# CBOX_ACCOUNT_RENEW="keychain item claude-token-<name>: store the new token there, then pipe it into cbox account add <name>"

# ─── voice ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Claude Code's /voice in the container. Needs PulseAudio on the Mac
# (brew install pulseaudio) and a claude.ai login.
# CBOX_AUDIO=1

# ─── image ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Folder with your own image additions for cbox rebuild: a dockerfile that
# starts with FROM claudebox (e.g. tmux, or Playwright + Chromium; see the
# README, "Your own additions to the image").
# CBOX_BUILD_DIR="$HOME/path/to/my-claudebox-additions"
